# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recon output — ALL of it is ignored. This repo publishes the *method*; the
# targets stay local.
#
# The earlier policy tracked `scope.md` + `notes.md` + `findings/` as "the
# durable record" and ignored a hand-written list of filenames. That was right
# while the repo was private. It is wrong now: `notes.md` on a real target is
# unpublished recon, and `scope.md` names the private program that pays for the
# finding. An allowlist also only protects the filenames somebody remembered —
# `ops-api-paths.txt` and `dnsx-raw.json` both slipped past it.
#
# So: blanket-ignore, one level deep. Anything under `recon/<host>/` stays out
# unless it is deliberately un-ignored here.
#
# Verify before you commit:  git status --ignored --short recon/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
recon/*/*

# recon/README.md documents the layout and stays tracked. It is one level deep,
# so recon/*/* does not match it. Per-target folders may keep a .gitkeep if an
# empty scaffold dir is wanted in the tree.
!recon/*/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials and capture material — never commit, ever, public repo or not.
# If you save a session cookie or a bearer token, it goes in a local file that
# is gitignored. notes.md must never contain a live token.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.keystore
credentials*
*cookie*.txt
*session*.json
secrets/

# Captured traffic and SSH key material. A .har file is a full session replay
# including every request header, which is a live token by another name.
*.har
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.cap
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
known_hosts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kali scratch — per AGENTS.md, work happens in /tmp/recon/<host> inside WSL and
# only finished files get copied back. Nothing here should ever land on D:.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tmp/
work/
scratch/

# One-shot probe scripts written into scripts/ by the PowerShell → bash recipe
# in docs/environment.md. Throwaway, and they inline machine-specific paths.
scripts/tmp-*
scripts/*.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling / editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
